    <item>
      <headword id="idp112440480">[Friday]</headword>
      <description>Tradition that was kept regarding Good Friday. Whether or not the potato crop had been planted before that day it was considered that at least two or three potatoes had to be planted on that day to ensure a good crop. Similarly peats were not cut on a Friday as it was thought this might bring death to the family concerned.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
